/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:507:* ''Research pair: the knock's leak'' (`W10`; its answer moves the dial's bytes, so it lands before the bake). MEASURED (two traded rounds, then a Mu test on the web, 2026-10-26; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w28-gate-lane">> #/the-knock-reading): IK already stands, so a dialer proves itself before any verdict; the floor knock harms nothing the floor promises; on the sovereign route a reader holding candidate pins and the clear path learns which of the K gates sharing an address and route a dial selects, at most log2(K) bits per dial, never the face, the verdict or a sealed byte; no public-pin filter escapes that, and a secret selector costs per-Nexus key delivery and a causal re-key on every removal. The operator ruled (2026-10-26) that the sovereign promise leaves a pin-holding path reader outside it, so `W10` closes as a named leak, with more research owed later.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:511:* `W26` The system wikis release and every other wiki reads the floor (#/rulings, 2026-10-16). Slice 1 stands (PR #49): genesis carries the first floor, its manifest and the `lares` and `lararium` snapshots by CID, and `@oracle` reads that floor by CID. Slice 2 stands (PR #52): each vessel's system, crossroads and realm pointers rest in its own `@catalog`, and nothing writes the shared `@oracle` after genesis (`oracle-doc-no-writer.test.ts`). Slice 3 stands (lane `--w26-floor-3`): the founding lands the counted 1-of-1 Kahu admission for persona zero's group (`landFoundingAdmission`) and registers `lares` and `lararium` as realm bags of the hearth's realm under persona zero's per-Nexus key (`landKahuRealm`); `kahuCabalCanonAccess` has its production caller (`kahuReachSourceOf`); the keel mounts only what the realm names, the registered bag set and the `bags/` mirrors follow, and no catalog row names a system bag. Slice 6 stands: one predicate (`requireKahuReach`) guards the residency reactor, meme put and delete, draft placement and a realm steward's write, and the keyholder island's verifier carries it for `--in-wiki` verbs. Slice 4 stands: the release (`floor-release`: body, CID, steward seal by a seated Kahu key, the cabal's high-impact approval of the manifest's exact bytes, the charter's epoch lineage), the chain fold, `lares nexus release`, the porch (`GET /floor/<Nexus AID>`, `/cas/<cid>` for the head's blobs), the browser's verified read, and the flow map's own `flow-pointer` domain in place of the retired `oracle-pointer`. The build runs six slices in order, under the architecture of #/rulings (2026-10-18), its shape and evidence at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w26-floor-lane">>: (1) the floor manifest and its read-face, genesis baking the first floor; (2) each vessel's pointers leave the shared document for its bootstrap, re-cutting `W21`; (3) the Kahu realm holds the live system documents, and a one-seat founding lands its 1-of-1 Kahu admission; (4) the release answer on the crossroads, folding `P8`; (5) the accept act per (face, Nexus), which follows Wave C's face context since its accepted floor rests as a face's D row; (6) reach into system canon refuses every hand outside the cabal. OWED: a browser Kahu hand rides Wave C's face context (the browser composes no board reader and reads as a stranger, fail closed); a sibling device of a seat-holding face reads the floor until that context carries the charter and the board to it; the carriage `canon` names (`device-admit.ts` `admitCanonDocs`, the browser's `hearth-canon`) read rows nothing writes now, and retire with `W21`'s rest. W.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:515:* `P10` The vessel-side fetch door stands built (`makeCidResolver` beside `hermCasTransitFromEnv` in `open-node-vessel.ts`); the herm's own client leg waits on the explicit-Nexus herm relay, since a herm dials no hearth. One circle in the law stands beside it: a carrier may read a book its registration declares public, the declaration lives on the realm doc, and the realm doc never crosses to a carrier. The held red in `tests/e2e/herm-reshares-public-blob.e2e.test.ts` waits on both. Also owed: seeding a herm from a stood Lararium. House. Before the fence where the ceremony seeds a herm.
