/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:587:* `F2` One recipe resolver (`surface-recipe.ts`) and the pool keyed by the whole session key (`mountSurface`) stand specified in mesh, with one proof through the node vessel's own parts that a recipe naming an offering resolves. Both platforms select plugins through its `resolveRecipePluginCids`; no production caller reaches `resolveSurfaceRecipe`. Owed: the node and browser compose sites resolve through the one function at surface mount; the wiki door (`mountWiki`), its retained mount specs and the recipe watch retire with the last caller; a surface island's events reach a verb gate bound to its session (`onSurfaceEvent`) when the node callers move (`F4`). O1.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:588:* `F6` The browser holder as owner, with unicast replies. Slice one stands (PR #56): a closed routing table (`holder-routes.ts`) sends each island message to exactly one port, a reply by its request id, camera traffic by its lease, the island's own asks to its owner port, and drops a kind with no route by name. Slice two stands (PR #58): every tab-to-holder message rides a random owner epoch, a session and a generation, and the holder refuses a stale or unknown one by name to that port alone; `session:open` with its face waits on `W4`'s face supplier. Slices three and four move the Repo and the daemon kernel into the holder; their sealed writes go to the asker (#/rulings, the asker seals). Slice three stands with `K15` step 3 (PR #81): the holder routes each sealed write to the session that caused it, and Chromium, which exposes no nested Worker inside a SharedWorker, takes the dedicated-worker floor, its swap waiting for the worker's `ready` before it replays the manifest and retiring the crossing it replaces. Slice four stays owed. O1.
