/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:656:* `P20` The carriage gates (`carriage-board.ts`, `vessel-raise.ts`, `nexus-carriage.ts`) count at the head alone, while `lares nexus members` honours anchored ancestry, so the list can show a member a gate does not yet honour. Built (PR #50): the carrier folds read the anchored lineage, and the contract writer cites the carried heads it supersedes across epochs for both families, so an uncarry, a roll and a re-carry read in order. Built (PR #54): a gate verifies a place contract carried across a charter roll in either direction, a newer gate walking the arm's roll anchors and an older gate accepting the presenter's charter epochs only where they extend its held lineage and pass `verifySealLineage`, each failing closed without its proof; the presenter assembles both, and `readBoardPresentation` folds with ancestry. The herm-mesh and mesh-scenarios witnesses join after A's boot roll. The held-out cell `herm-mesh-roll` (PR #57) rolls A's charter between two herm joins after the boot serves, each herm naming its own head, and presents the opening carry at the rolled head twice: under A's own roll anchor it verifies, and under the same anchor parts signed outside the seats it falls silent by place-contract name. P19's cabal half stays parked on `--gate-ancestry`. P.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:657:* `W18` The founding hearth's carriage fold walks the roll anchors (PR #50): after a charter roll, the carrier folds at the carriage pull's refresh, `placeCarriedNexuses`, the membership refold and the carry-bundle take count every act the anchored lineage carries, and count none without an anchor (`carriageAncestryFromBoard`; red and controls in `carrier-fold-across-roll.test.ts`). Held-out herm-mesh and the nexus cell then read A filing all four pins and verifying relay-2, and with `P20`'s gate half (PR #54) both read green. W.
