/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:898:<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract">> session contract orders one session's capabilities and switch
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:16:role              = "session-contract — the contract a SESSION holds with the vessel it rides: one vessel owns one durable Repo, one store lock, custody and one trusted face-blind daemon; each browser tab or CLI run opens a volatile session that wears exactly one verified face. An owner-minted id ROUTES and nothing more; a binding and worker-held capabilities AUTHORIZE; a generation advances at a switch. The owner persists switch acts and request outcomes and never a roster of sessions. Every interactive surface takes its own island, a session-scoped document view replaces the broad sync port, one function resolves the effective recipe at surface mount, the holder answers the requesting binding alone, and receipts bind to the face's proof subject. Every hand (a tab, a CLI run, the disk watcher, a spirit's seat) opens a session and differs by capability profile, never by key. Carries the five-step switch, how a session ends, what the code holds, and the twelve debts of the build"
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:30:''A session wears the face and the vessel wears none'' (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/persona-policy#/the-session">>). This carrier states the contract under that ruling: what a session carries, what the vessel's owner keeps for it, how a surface mounts, how the holder speaks, and how a session switches and ends.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:34:> ''Register.'' The operator approved this contract's decisions as presented (operator ruling, 2026-10-11; quote license: //"Pono, this all reads good. Flowstate approved (per tab state reads pono, we want that, and can sync up 'views' later if needed)."//). A sentence below that carries the operator's own words stands as law. The remainder reads as ''the designed shape'': approved in outline, and unbuilt wherever #/standing-and-owed says OWED. One reading belongs to the house and carries its own mark (#/receipts).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:40:!! What a session carries ~ an id that routes, a binding that authorizes
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:45:| `generation` | a counter that advances at a switch; an effect of an earlier generation never lands in a later one | |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:46:| `face` | the resolved face, immutable within one generation: the PersonaGroup, its proof subject, its verified admit, the causal revision the relation stood at, and the absolute ids of its four planes (`@persona` · `@circles` · `@identities` · `@sessions`) | a persona root, or any root bytes |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:48:| `state` | `opening` · `live` · `switching` · `revoked` · `closing` · `closed` | |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:51:''The id routes; the binding and the worker-held capabilities authorize.'' The sovereign worker verifies custody or delegation, the admit, the proof subject, the plane derivation and the relation's observed state. The owner then mints the id and binds it to the pending port or socket. Every later message gets checked against that binding before it routes, and the worker checks the bound facet and the verb.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:61:''Every hand that reaches a vessel opens a session, and a session wears one face'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-12, approved as presented). A hand names WHO moved; the face names the relation the move speaks in. Hands differ by capability profile. No hand holds a key, and no second kind of identity stands beside the face.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:80:* ''The Mask travels as authorship.'' A write into a shared realm carries the hand that made it as a field of the record, beside the face that signs: the kind of hand, and a spirit's Mask. The field names and authorizes nothing; no gate reads it. A Mask pins to no key and no identifier, so it counts as no pet-name (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/persona-policy">>).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:82:* ''A projected wiki stands as a surface.'' One tree on disk serves the person. A wiki names a face's relation to a composition (#/the-working-layer), so each face's wiki takes its own folder and the path says whose wiki it holds. No file and no `.meta` chooses the signer: an edit returns under the face of the session that leases the surface. A switch advances the generation, and an edit sensed under an earlier generation surfaces as a draft.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:85:''The door carries; the hand authorizes'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-12, approved as presented). MCP and the CLI stand as two doors onto one contract: the same session messages over the one socket, one verb table, the same named refusals, the same receipts. Parity belongs to the doors. A profile belongs to the hand, and no door widens or narrows it.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:88:* ''A seat never signs an act that changes who holds authority'' (an attended spirit acts as the operator, so this bound falls on a standing one alone): a vault or custody verb, an admit, a kapae, a quorum signature, a face switch, or a residency move into a bag. A seat MAY draft such an act for a person to sign.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:92:> ''Two house readings, marked as such.'' A file moved by hand between two faces' folders arrives as a copy under the destination's face, asked for by name, and never as a silent change of signer. And the house publishes this limit: //facets on one operator's disk hold separate network identities and signing authority; anyone who can inspect that disk or its copies may read their projections and link the facets, and writing style or timing may also link them.//
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:102:The working layer follows the wiki across recipe recomposition; it never follows the recipe's composition fingerprint. Here, `wiki` names the face's relation to a composition over bags, never a global wiki name or registry id. Two faces at one table may hold wikis that share bags; sharing happens at the bag. Presence and multiplayer spaces sit above shared bags.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:116:''The vessel's owner keeps its live routes in memory alone.'' It persists two things: the switch ACTS, vessel-private, and the durable OUTCOMES of requests. It MUST NOT persist a list of live sessions. A roster of sessions would stand as a record of which faces one vessel wore together, which the session ruling forbids from reaching any wire and which nothing needs at rest.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:126:!! Islands ~ one per interactive surface, and per-tab state as wanted
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:128:''Every interactive wiki surface takes its own island.'' The island's key reads `(sessionId, generation, surfaceId, wikiId, facePlaneId, recipeRevision, capabilityProfile)`. A key of wiki and face alone falls short: two tabs wearing one face still carry two writers and two sets of control state.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:142:''Session islands hold ephemeral replicas; the vessel's owner alone persists.'' No durable per-island store survives a session. A plane address a caller supplies grants nothing: the view answers from the session's own facets.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:148:> ''Four house readings, marked as such.'' ''A bag reaches a session read-only'': a session writes its wiki's working, personal and draft layers and its face's own planes, and a move into a bag runs as an owner-side verb, never as an island's sync write. ''One table of profile against layer decides a write'': a seat writes the working layer alone, and the watcher writes the working layer and surfaces drafts. ''Content opens by reference'': a session reads the content its recipe names and the content a document it may read references; the owner's store answers, and bytes that fail to recompute to their address never leave. ''An island settles before it goes'': a session island keeps no store, so at an orderly close it names the heads it holds and waits until the owner holds them; a switch or a revocation closes its channel first.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:152:<<~ ahu #/the-effective-recipe>>
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:154:!! The effective recipe ~ one function, at surface mount
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:156:''One mesh function resolves a session's effective recipe when a surface mounts.'' It takes the vessel's recipe records, the session's verified face plane, the bags that face may read, the plugin inputs and the capability profile; it returns absolute ids and a recipe revision. A grant decides what a face CAN read and a recipe decides what a session DOES mount (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm#/the-house-table">>).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:158:''A mounted island never hot-swaps.'' A recipe change gets written, sync carries it, and the next mount reads it. Node and browser share the one function; neither platform resolves a recipe of its own.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:162:> ''A house reading, marked as one.'' A recipe that names a bag its face holds no grant to read refuses the mount by that bag's name. The house table rules that a recipe narrows a view and never widens a grant; the refusal, where a silent skip could also have kept that law, belongs to the house: a mount that quietly lays less than its recipe names would read as the whole wiki.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:170:''Every message after the open carries `ownerEpoch`, `sessionId` and `generation`.'' Shape and kind discriminate a message; no field names a format number, and the generation counts switches alone. A request adds `requestId`; surface traffic adds `surfaceId` and, where a mount matters, `mountEpoch`. A reply returns to the originating binding alone. The holder broadcasts nothing.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:173:| `session:open` → `session:opened` / `session:refused` | A request id and an explicit local face reference. The answer carries the owner epoch, the minted id, the generation, a safe face reference and the facet labels, and never a root or a general signer. A faceless vessel boots over a separate maintenance channel that grants no content session. |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:175:| `session:surface-open` → `session:surface-ready` | A surface kind and a wiki or camera reference. The owner resolves the recipe, opens a scoped view, then leases the island. |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:179:| `session:switch` → `session:switch-result` | The expected generation and the target face reference. It advances this session alone. |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:186:<<~ ahu #/receipts>>
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:188:!! Receipts ~ bound to the face's proof subject and the input's digest
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:190:''A request's outcome rests with the face's proof subject and the digest of its input.'' A receipt bound to the session that asked would strand a one-shot CLI run, whose session ends with its process. So a ''newly verified session wearing the same face'' reads the receipt by request id, and a session wearing another face reads nothing. Cancel, unknown-outcome and no-silent-redispatch hold as they stand. An explicit vessel audit facet may read across faces; an ordinary session never inherits it.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:203:* ''`persona wear` switches the caller's LIVE session.'' An interactive CLI keeps that face until it exits.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:206:The local socket carries the open, calls, receipt queries, cancel, switch and close on a socket-bound session.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:232:''A browser vessel's trust domain runs at one custody context'': one browser profile under one locked OS account, holding one vessel's store, lock and keys. The browser walls storage, locks, workers and channels between profiles and accounts, and walls nothing inside one origin of one profile; a profile walls storage, never people, since anyone at an unlocked OS login can switch to it. So a household's shared device gives each operator their own locked OS account and browser profile, and the vessel never counts humans: no constructor for a human exists in the model (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/persona-circle">>), and a ''hand'' names a session's custody principal (#/the-hands), never a person.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:238:''Tiers contract outward by signed, narrowed relations.'' One operator's household Nexus, neighbourhood Lararium, tribe and regional Nexus stand as distinct realms, charters and seats over one vessel or several. Carriage carries and reads nothing; a seat, a realm membership, a document read and a promotion each take their own grant, and no tier inherits another's membership or map by transit. Tiers sharing one origin, host or relay can correlate by metadata; where tiers must not learn of each other, they run on separate substrate. The research rests at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/browser-trust-line-2026">>.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:246:* ''A CLI run'': the socket closes or the process exits; an explicit close; a switch; an observed causal revocation.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:247:* ''A tab'': the page's close signal; a lost port; the holder's death; a switch; an observed causal revocation.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:255:<<~ ahu #/the-switch>>
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:257:!! The switch ~ five steps, one session
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:259:# ''Freeze and preflight.'' New calls on this session freeze. The owner preflights the target face's custody or delegation, admit, causal relation, absolute planes, proof subject and effective recipes, as immutable descriptions. It MUST NOT mount the target face before the old facets fall: one session would then hold two live face views. A refused preflight leaves the old generation live.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:260:# ''Write the intent.'' A vessel-private switch intent gets written and flushed: the causal position, the outgoing face and the incoming face.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:261:# ''Fence the old generation.'' Its dials stop, its operation and signer facets fall, its scoped document channels close, and its surfaces and islands dispose. An effect in flight resolves through its durable receipt.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:262:# ''Advance, mount, dial.'' The generation advances. The target surfaces mount under the new scoped view, and the session dials with fresh keys under the target face's proof.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:278:* ''A holder that answers the asker and fences its epoch, faceless.'' The shared holder delivers each island message by one closed route table (`packages/lararium-browser/src/holder-routes.ts`): a reply to the port that asked, camera traffic to the port that leases the camera, the island's own asks to the port whose manifest it took; it drops the rest by name and broadcasts nothing. It mints one random `ownerEpoch` per boot and one random `sessionId` per port, greets each port with its envelope, and refuses by name, to that port alone, a message with no envelope, another owner's epoch, an unknown session, another port's session or another generation; the island sees no envelope (`packages/lararium-browser/src/shared-holder-core.ts`, the tab's half in `shared-holder.ts`). These sessions carry the maintenance channel and wear no face.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:284:* ''The hands' profiles.'' `face`, `verb`, `ingest` and `seat` (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/session-contract.ts`). A session carries one from its open to its end, and a switch of face keeps it.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:286:* ''The one recipe resolver'' (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/surface-recipe.ts`). It returns absolute ids and a revision at surface mount.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:287:* ''The pool's surface door'' (`mountSurface`). It keys an island by the whole session key, opens the view over exactly what the recipe resolved, and hands the island no store, no catalog, no disk mirror and none of the vessel's own doors. A surface island's events take a door of their own and never the one that places vessel verbs. `closeSession` ends a session in good order and `fenceSession` closes its views first; from either, the session mounts nothing again.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:288:* ''The face a session wears, and its signer'' (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/session-face.ts`, `session-signer.ts`, over `face-authority.ts` and `face-proof-subjects.ts`). One function joins a verified chain, this vessel's own key for the face, the admit's verdict and the PersonaGroup's private grant into the `face` value, and derives the proof subject and the four planes itself; a signer mints for one live session, asks the owner's table before every signature, and drops at a close or a switch.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:289:* ''The island's half'' (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/sovereign-kernel.ts`, `view-channel.ts`). An island whose manifest carries a view stands under the minted peer id, lays the resolved slots, asks its view for catalog names and content, runs no recipe watch, and settles its writes before it acks a teardown.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:293:# ''The contract in mesh.'' The session type, its validators, the port and socket binding, and refusal of a stale owner epoch or generation.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:295:# ''The face proof and its grants.'' Two faces on one vessel present different proof subjects, and a copied id or an own-hand claim gains no plane (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof">>). The subjects, private authority, the session signer and the one face supplier stand specified in code. The debt closes when the node's session open on the local socket and the browser holder call the supplier and mint a signer at every open. Those callers wait on three things: the custody rows for the face proof key and each vessel's face-scoped key, an admit that signs what it carries, and the ring's lookup by face subject (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof#/owed">>). The supplier's face names one PersonaGroup at one Nexus; a face at two Nexuses waits on this contract's word.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:296:# ''The recipe resolver and the pool's identity.'' The working-layer binding follows #/the-working-layer; two same-face sessions take two islands, a repeated exact mount opens one, and a recipe write reaches the next mount by sync without changing a live mount. The resolver and the whole-key pool stand specified in code, with one proof through the node vessel's own parts that a recipe naming an offering resolves. The working-layer binding stays owed and waits on the join door, where the face secret arrives. The callers stay owed too: the compose sites resolve through the one function at surface mount, the browser's plugin selection folds into it, and the wiki door, its retained mount specs and the recipe watch retire with the last caller.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:297:# ''Node callers move to sessions.'' Two CLI sessions wear different faces at once over one Repo; a copied socket and a cross-face receipt read both refuse; a same-face receipt reads after the CLI that asked has exited.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:298:# ''The browser holder as owner.'' Two tabs show one backing Repo and one held lock; a failed daemon boot refuses both, releases the lock and permits a retry. The routing and the faceless envelope stand (#/standing-and-owed). The face-bearing `session:open`, `session:call` and `session:switch` wait on the face supplier's browser caller, `W4` (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road#/the-loops">>), and the holder's custody fork waits on the operator.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:300:# ''The switch, and the selector retires.'' Switching one session leaves another live; an old generation's effect never paints the new face; no boot path reads a vessel-wide active face.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:301:# ''The disk as a surface.'' The watcher opens a session and leases each projected wiki; a disk edit returns under the leasing session's face; an edit from an earlier generation and a file changed under no lease both surface as drafts; a move between two faces' folders asks for a copy by name.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:303:# ''The Mask as authorship.'' A record written into a shared realm carries its kind of hand, and a spirit's Mask, as a field no gate reads; a session cannot write another hand's mark.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:317:<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm#/the-house-table">>

