    79	* ''A standing grant names the face a seat wears.'' The grant rests at the MCP mount. The owner verifies it afresh at every open, and it opens nothing while the vessel rests at the floor: no spirit works on a locked vessel.
    80	* ''The Mask travels as authorship.'' A write into a shared realm carries the hand that made it as a field of the record, beside the face that signs: the kind of hand, and a spirit's Mask. The field names and authorizes nothing; no gate reads it. A Mask pins to no key and no identifier, so it counts as no pet-name (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/persona-policy">>).
    81	* ''An agent's dissent drafts; a person's ask edits'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-16). An agent that disagrees with a person's edit files its own version as a draft beside it, and the person's edit stands until the person chooses: an agent never overrides. A person who asks an agent to edit a tiddler directly makes that edit the person's own act (the ''attended'' position above), and the agent writes it, reaching only the tiddlers the ask names and only under the asker's own write authority.
    82	* ''A projected wiki stands as a surface.'' One tree on disk serves the person. A wiki names a face's relation to a composition (#/the-working-layer), so each face's wiki takes its own folder and the path says whose wiki it holds. No file and no `.meta` chooses the signer: an edit returns under the face of the session that leases the surface. A switch advances the generation, and an edit sensed under an earlier generation surfaces as a draft.
    83	* ''Files that changed while no session held the lease'' ingest at the next mount, under the mounting face, as surfaced drafts.
    84	
    85	''The door carries; the hand authorizes'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-12, approved as presented). MCP and the CLI stand as two doors onto one contract: the same session messages over the one socket, one verb table, the same named refusals, the same receipts. Parity belongs to the doors. A profile belongs to the hand, and no door widens or narrows it.
    86	
    87	* ''One verb table serves every hand.'' A seat sees every verb, and a verb beyond its profile refuses by name.
    88	* ''A seat never signs an act that changes who holds authority'' (an attended spirit acts as the operator, so this bound falls on a standing one alone): a vault or custody verb, an admit, a kapae, a quorum signature, a face switch, or a residency move into a bag. A seat MAY draft such an act for a person to sign.
    89	* ''Authority only narrows down a chain of spirits.'' A spirit MAY seat a sub-spirit under a profile no wider than its own, and the Mask records the chain.
    90	* ''A container makes the profile bind.'' A spirit that shares its operator's OS account reaches every door that operator reaches, and its declared hand stays a declaration. A spirit that runs in a container holding only its seat's socket and grant holds no other door.
    98	!! The working layer ~ one document per face relation, wiki, and slot kind
    99	
   100	One working document follows each `(face relation, wiki, slot kind)`. Its address derives from a secret held only by that face's vessels; no binding record or mint race decides the address. Two vessels mounting offline derive one document and merge their writes.
   101	
   102	The working layer follows the wiki across recipe recomposition; it never follows the recipe's composition fingerprint. Here, `wiki` names the face's relation to a composition over bags, never a global wiki name or registry id. Two faces at one table may hold wikis that share bags; sharing happens at the bag. Presence and multiplayer spaces sit above shared bags.
   103	
   104	A leaf with an admit and no seat writes nothing to the face's wikis. Join first; the face secret arrives at the face-proof join (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof#/the-chain">>).
   105	
   106	The gate and document membership refuse a removed vessel. The working document keeps its address; rotation to a fresh document takes a separate, deliberate act.
   107	
   108	The resolver keys bindings by `prefix/fingerprint` and stores them through `daemonStore` (`packages/lararium-keyhive/src/resolve-binding.ts`). The working document follows this address law instead of that binding map.
