   126	!! Islands ~ one per interactive surface, and per-tab state as wanted
   127	
   128	''Every interactive wiki surface takes its own island.'' The island's key reads `(sessionId, generation, surfaceId, wikiId, facePlaneId, recipeRevision, capabilityProfile)`. A key of wiki and face alone falls short: two tabs wearing one face still carry two writers and two sets of control state.
   129	
   130	''Per-tab state stands as the operator wants it'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-11; quote license: //"per tab state reads pono, we want that, and can sync up 'views' later if needed"//). Each tab runs its own TiddlyWiki engine and keeps its own story river, drafts, scroll, cameras and frames. Two tabs of one face share their durable documents through the one owner. Syncing a view across tabs stays a later, optional feature, and nothing in this contract waits on it.
   131	
   132	''A camera's frame keys and revisions live within its surface mount'' (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom#/the-ruling">>). The pool's bookkeeping, pending calls, failure accounting and leases all use the whole key.
