   153	
   154	!! The effective recipe ~ one function, at surface mount
   155	
   156	''One mesh function resolves a session's effective recipe when a surface mounts.'' It takes the vessel's recipe records, the session's verified face plane, the bags that face may read, the plugin inputs and the capability profile; it returns absolute ids and a recipe revision. A grant decides what a face CAN read and a recipe decides what a session DOES mount (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm#/the-house-table">>).
   157	
   158	''A mounted island never hot-swaps.'' A recipe change gets written, sync carries it, and the next mount reads it. Node and browser share the one function; neither platform resolves a recipe of its own.
   159	
   160	''The revision names what a mount lays'': the slots with the documents they resolved to, the engine core and the plugin selection. Two mounts share a revision exactly when they would lay the same island.
   161	
   162	> ''A house reading, marked as one.'' A recipe that names a bag its face holds no grant to read refuses the mount by that bag's name. The house table rules that a recipe narrows a view and never widens a grant; the refusal, where a silent skip could also have kept that law, belongs to the house: a mount that quietly lays less than its recipe names would read as the whole wiki.
