   188	!! Receipts ~ bound to the face's proof subject and the input's digest
   189	
   190	''A request's outcome rests with the face's proof subject and the digest of its input.'' A receipt bound to the session that asked would strand a one-shot CLI run, whose session ends with its process. So a ''newly verified session wearing the same face'' reads the receipt by request id, and a session wearing another face reads nothing. Cancel, unknown-outcome and no-silent-redispatch hold as they stand. An explicit vessel audit facet may read across faces; an ordinary session never inherits it.
   191	
   192	> ''A house reading, marked as one.'' One vessel-wide outcome document MAY hold several faces' results while each session reads only its own face's. The operator's ruling supports the reading (plane isolation runs by capability-limited sessions under a trusted daemon, so the daemon may hold what no single session may read); the operator ruled the isolation bound and never this document's shape.
