   257	!! The switch ~ five steps, one session
   258	
   259	# ''Freeze and preflight.'' New calls on this session freeze. The owner preflights the target face's custody or delegation, admit, causal relation, absolute planes, proof subject and effective recipes, as immutable descriptions. It MUST NOT mount the target face before the old facets fall: one session would then hold two live face views. A refused preflight leaves the old generation live.
   260	# ''Write the intent.'' A vessel-private switch intent gets written and flushed: the causal position, the outgoing face and the incoming face.
   261	# ''Fence the old generation.'' Its dials stop, its operation and signer facets fall, its scoped document channels close, and its surfaces and islands dispose. An effect in flight resolves through its durable receipt.
   262	# ''Advance, mount, dial.'' The generation advances. The target surfaces mount under the new scoped view, and the session dials with fresh keys under the target face's proof.
   263	# ''Write the outcome.'' A mount or a dial that fails at commit closes this session and reports the partial outcome; the caller opens afresh. Nothing restores the old face's authority in silence.
   264	
   265	''Every other session and the daemon continue untouched.'' The record never crosses the wire (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/persona-policy#/the-session">>).
   266	
   284	* ''The hands' profiles.'' `face`, `verb`, `ingest` and `seat` (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/session-contract.ts`). A session carries one from its open to its end, and a switch of face keeps it.
   285	* ''The scoped document view'' (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/session-document-view.ts` over `gated-sync-leg.ts`). It answers announcements, fetches, writes, catalog names and content reads from the session's own facets.
   286	* ''The one recipe resolver'' (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/surface-recipe.ts`). It returns absolute ids and a revision at surface mount.
   287	* ''The pool's surface door'' (`mountSurface`). It keys an island by the whole session key, opens the view over exactly what the recipe resolved, and hands the island no store, no catalog, no disk mirror and none of the vessel's own doors. A surface island's events take a door of their own and never the one that places vessel verbs. `closeSession` ends a session in good order and `fenceSession` closes its views first; from either, the session mounts nothing again.
   288	* ''The face a session wears, and its signer'' (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/session-face.ts`, `session-signer.ts`, over `face-authority.ts` and `face-proof-subjects.ts`). One function joins a verified chain, this vessel's own key for the face, the admit's verdict and the PersonaGroup's private grant into the `face` value, and derives the proof subject and the four planes itself; a signer mints for one live session, asks the owner's table before every signature, and drops at a close or a switch.
   289	* ''The island's half'' (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/sovereign-kernel.ts`, `view-channel.ts`). An island whose manifest carries a view stands under the minted peer id, lays the resolved slots, asks its view for catalog names and content, runs no recipe watch, and settles its writes before it acks a teardown.
   290	
   291	''OWED ~ twelve debts, each resting on the one before it.'' A builder closes each with its callers and its own proof, so the tree keeps a runnable contract at every step.
   292	
   293	# ''The contract in mesh.'' The session type, its validators, the port and socket binding, and refusal of a stale owner epoch or generation.
   294	# ''Scoped document access.'' The session-scoped view over announcements, fetches, writes, catalog and content-addressed reads; no durable per-island store. The view, the pool's surface door and the island's half stand specified in code. The debt closes when every interactive surface mounts through that door, which waits on a verified face (debt three) and on callers that hold a session (debts five and seven). Four hunks close with it: the share verdict's caller reads the pool's view for an island's peer, the leaf's relay adapter wears the one-way gate over its hearth's canon, the hearth wears that gate's twin toward its leaves, and a wiki island's verbs that read the catalog document move to the view's catalog ask.
   295	# ''The face proof and its grants.'' Two faces on one vessel present different proof subjects, and a copied id or an own-hand claim gains no plane (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof">>). The subjects, private authority, the session signer and the one face supplier stand specified in code. The debt closes when the node's session open on the local socket and the browser holder call the supplier and mint a signer at every open. Those callers wait on three things: the custody rows for the face proof key and each vessel's face-scoped key, an admit that signs what it carries, and the ring's lookup by face subject (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof#/owed">>). The supplier's face names one PersonaGroup at one Nexus; a face at two Nexuses waits on this contract's word.
   296	# ''The recipe resolver and the pool's identity.'' The working-layer binding follows #/the-working-layer; two same-face sessions take two islands, a repeated exact mount opens one, and a recipe write reaches the next mount by sync without changing a live mount. The resolver and the whole-key pool stand specified in code, with one proof through the node vessel's own parts that a recipe naming an offering resolves. The working-layer binding stays owed and waits on the join door, where the face secret arrives. The callers stay owed too: the compose sites resolve through the one function at surface mount, the browser's plugin selection folds into it, and the wiki door, its retained mount specs and the recipe watch retire with the last caller.
   297	# ''Node callers move to sessions.'' Two CLI sessions wear different faces at once over one Repo; a copied socket and a cross-face receipt read both refuse; a same-face receipt reads after the CLI that asked has exited.
   298	# ''The browser holder as owner.'' Two tabs show one backing Repo and one held lock; a failed daemon boot refuses both, releases the lock and permits a retry. The routing and the faceless envelope stand (#/standing-and-owed). The face-bearing `session:open`, `session:call` and `session:switch` wait on the face supplier's browser caller, `W4` (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road#/the-loops">>), and the holder's custody fork waits on the operator.
   299	# ''Browser surfaces.'' Two tabs mount one wiki under separate sessions; frames and control answers reach their source surface alone; no wiki engine runs on the page's main thread.
   300	# ''The switch, and the selector retires.'' Switching one session leaves another live; an old generation's effect never paints the new face; no boot path reads a vessel-wide active face.
   301	# ''The disk as a surface.'' The watcher opens a session and leases each projected wiki; a disk edit returns under the leasing session's face; an edit from an earlier generation and a file changed under no lease both surface as drafts; a move between two faces' folders asks for a copy by name.
   302	# ''The seat.'' An MCP connection opens a session under a standing grant, verified at each open and refused at the floor; its profile writes the working layer alone.
   303	# ''The Mask as authorship.'' A record written into a shared realm carries its kind of hand, and a spirit's Mask, as a field no gate reads; a session cannot write another hand's mark.
   304	# ''Door parity at the session.'' A CLI run and an MCP connection open the same session kinds and draw the same named refusals; a seat's refused verb names its profile; a seat drafts an authority act and cannot sign one; a sub-spirit's profile never exceeds its parent's.
   305	
   306	''A flipped bound reopens the design.'' Should the operator ever rule the daemon untrusted, faces take per-face encryption with decryption beyond the daemon. Should hostile same-origin code enter scope, capability use moves behind a stronger boundary. Should shared engine state across tabs become wanted, a serialized multi-surface writer gets defined before any island key collapses.
   100	* ''A working Lararium comes first'': Live Wiki Browser -><- Live Node, under manual QA on one machine. Sensorium work waits behind that milestone.
   101	* ''A founding road carries its own succession.'' A reconstitution kit lets another competent operator stand a node and read its grammar; a rite held in one operator's head alone carries no succession.
   102	* ''Face plurality stands as a day-one requirement.'' Each of the two humans wears at least three faces, each with a public Handle, on the first Nexus.
   103	
   104	!!! The house as a container
   105	* ''All CODE runs dockerized''; the host keeps only the hooks into the operator's environment (files and bags, session capture, the editor and CLI entry, custody).
   106	* ''ONE Lararium per HUMAN, never per face.'' A human's faces keep their data together in one vessel (`PRIVATE-all, PUBLIC-one`); the recorded face-switch act carries plurality. No design assumes a container or a state mount per face.
   107	* ''A SESSION wears the face; the vessel wears none'' (operator-ruled; quote license: //"a human might want a tab open as one Persona, and a tab open as another Persona... same vessel. Identity as relation."// and //"a CLI session wears its own face too … those act as ephemeral UX"//). A vessel holds its roots and one store. A session — a browser tab, a CLI run — contracts in as ONE persona, and several sessions may live at once over one vessel, each wearing its own. Every act carries exactly one face. Two faces live from one vessel never link on the wire: each session proves itself under its own face-scoped key, never under a key the vessel shares across them. The vessel-wide parts (custody, the daemon island) serve every session and let none read another's planes.
   108	* ''Local-first first.'' Cloud "backup larariums" under other humans' delegated keys stand DEFERRED until the operator can deploy to a cloud surface. Nothing in the container or the face-switch work may foreclose a keyless ciphertext carrier later.
   109	* ''The boundary'' (settled by the house under those rulings): one multi-arch image; `/workspace` mounts bags and wikis, `/state` mounts vessel homes and custody, never an image layer; the local socket stays INSIDE the container and the host CLI enters through `docker compose exec`; the app never receives the docker socket; mDNS offers unauthoritative LAN candidates and a pinned admission alone grants authority; DNS-01 wildcard TLS supplies browser secure contexts; a release manifest binds the image digest to the genesis, engine and grammar CIDs.
   110	
   111	!!! No global now
   112	* ''A wall clock never decides whether an act runs.'' Abandonment, revocation and expiry ride causal events; a timer serves only its holder's own liveness, and a device clock may sit under an adversary's hand. Web2.5 timers (TLS acceptance, OAuth tokens) sit at the edge of the causal island.
   113	* ''Lapse rides a causal fence'': an epoch roll, a burn marker, or causal supersession at a verified relation fence. A replica missing that history reports an incomplete view, never "expired"; quiet never means lapse.
   114	
   115	!!! The Stable state and its consequences
   116	* ''Every Lararium holds a charter.'' One operator's charter reads as a SEED and two operators' seats in one charter read as a NEXUS (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/kahu#/seed-and-nexus">>). A household seed never grows into a Nexus; a Nexus founds fresh at threshold two of two. One "I" may hold several PersonaGroups. A Nexus grows by adding seats through its own rolls.
   117	* ''A household seed serves its holder alone.'' A one-operator seed gives durable use without recruiting a mesh; useful local standing precedes every wider relation.
   118	* ''Guests walk the household seed.'' Planes stay persona-scoped, so a guest sees its own documents, the public and infrastructure shelf, and every realm its worn face stands in; a face may stand in many, as a person belongs to many clubs, and a guest's other faces stand in none of them.
   119	* ''Add-a-face (A).'' The daemon writes the public half; the terminal seals the recovery share; seating stays a separate act.
   120	* ''Every leaf starts at the floor with its own root.'' A human may later JOIN a leaf to a PersonaGroup so its devices sync as one fleet; joining never takes the device's own root away.
   121	* ''Founding persona zero belongs to standing'', never to a later verb. A capable vessel founds its household seed, so a "vessel with no charter" reads Mu.
   122	* ''Stable folds into the re-found'' as its core.
   123	* ''Forks report per board'': every presenter names every fork on the board it reads (the KERI watcher shape).
   124	
   125	!!! Planes ~ cabal, realm, Nexus
   126	* ''CABAL names the collective, REALM holds shared resources, NEXUS names the federated hardware mesh.'' The Nexus `@crossroads` board serves public-infrastructure docs and the Kahu Cabal keeps them. An operator's offering to a book club belongs in that club's realm, signed by the face worn there.
   127	* ''Kahu drafts in the realm the charter derives''; publishing to `@crossroads` stands as a separate, recorded promotion act. A second Kahu realm gets made only for a genuinely different relation.
   128	* ''Promotion approves the EXACT BYTES'' (hash, purpose, surface) under a threshold the charter sets, with a higher bar for charter, admission and trust-root changes. A CID, a clerk's edit or an active persona never stands in for collective approval.
   129	* ''Steward signing.'' A scoped face signs acts that belong to one person; a transparent quorum Handle signs acts the collective owns; the root never appears publicly. A human wears MANY faces and many public Handles, each in many cabals, and signs a steward edge with the face or Handle worn IN THAT CABAL.
   130	* ''Oracle answer'': one public answer per Nexus, signed by that Nexus's Kahu steward; a herm carries and presents it and signs nothing public. The engine floor rides as one shared content-addressed bake, and each answer names its floor CID (operator ruling).
   131	* ''Herm tending'': tending may reach the herm's key; the house accepts that reach and names it (operator ruling).
   132	* ''Introduction and admission'': a user introduces; an operator admits; the answer consumes the introduction (operator ruling).
   133	* ''Names and counters'': a counter orders one writer's own emissions only, and the face lives at the session capability. The per-Nexus convergence secret and its keyring leave the model: nothing derives from one, the Stable founding act yields none, no seat act commits to one and no admission delivers one. (operator ruling; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/cap-tier#/key-delivery">>).
   134	* ''Kahu acts fall into four chartered classes'': ordinary (1-of-1); high-impact — charter, admission, trust root (3-of-5, or 2-of-3 for a small body); emergency (2-of-3, a narrow pre-authorized power reviewed by a later causal act); revocation (the threshold of the original act). A challenge appends to the record and may pause LOCAL reliance; it never halts the protocol. Admission of a Kahu or a Lamplighter always takes the seat quorum, and no ordinary single-seat class covers it; kapae and rolls take the quorum too; the user road rides its own bound (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/kahu#/seed-and-nexus">>).
   135	* ''Renewal runs as three sequences, kept apart'' (the realm feed, a per-renewal causal position, the KEL), and lapse arrives as three distinct events: signed departure, recorded removal by relation-scoped kapae, renewal supersession.
   136	* ''A cancel crossing a herm yields three receipts'': the caller's abandonment, the relay's delivery (transit only), the vessel's outcome. A caller timeout never counts as a cancel; eviction answers `retention-gap`.
   137	* ''One face at a time names WHO ANSWERS for an act.'' The switch law reads in `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/persona-policy#/one-face`.
   138	* ''A session wears the face; the vessel wears none'' (operator ruling).
   186	* ''The hands'': every hand opens a session. A tasked spirit comes down to an AI, a Mask and the vessel's seat, attended or standing; the vessel's own key serves as a spirit's system identity; a Mask counts as no pet-name. The door carries and the hand authorizes, over one verb table, and a standing seat never signs an act that changes who holds authority (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract#/the-hands">>).
   187	* ''Sealed-row acts ride the custody door'', never a store verb whose output lands in the daemon's document in the clear (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/waking-floor#/the-shape">>).
   188	* ''Gate keys come in three tiers'': a floor route's keys derive from the floor key, and a sovereign route's from the sealed custody root (operator ruling); the serving route's bundle derives from SK, a third tier that leaves those two untouched (#/rulings, the ember's serving gate). A faceless place takes a fourth arm at the gate, the place arm, and a session opens before its certificate. The floor key rests outside the vessel key, and the face proof names what a holder of the disk without the passphrase reaches and never reaches (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof#/the-gate-exchange">>).
   189	* ''The widget render boundary stands withdrawn'', and the parser carries recovery (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/graceful-parsing">>).
