   191	!!! Operator rulings, 2026-10-16 ~ approved as the controller's story leans
   192	* ''A joined device reads the hearth's corpus and keeps its own.'' A joinee mounts the hearth's `@lararium` corpus read-only beside its own, and its writes stay in its own; the oracle plane (the hearth's catalog, daemon doc and faces' planes) never crosses (`device-admit.ts#admitCanonDocs`). Row `W21` carries the build.
   193	* ''The bag plane hides its creator before strangers carry it.'' The carried bag event's creator identifier in the clear gets measured red-first and ranked before wave three: ahead of anything that lets a third human's data cross a herm. Row `W25`.
   194	* ''An agent's dissent drafts; a person's ask edits'' (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract">> #/the-hands): an agent never overrides a person's edit, and a person's direct ask to edit a tiddler makes the edit the person's own act, bounded by the ask and the asker's authority.
   195	* ''The system wikis release; every other wiki reads the floor'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-16). Only each Nexus's Kahu cabal writes the `lares` and `lararium` wikis and bags live. Every other wiki, and every other hand, mounts them read-only by CID: the latest release that cabal approved. The release rides the Nexus's crossroads board as its public answer, naming the floor CID under the Kahu steward's seal. The cabal approves the exact bytes under its charter's threshold, and a herm carries the answer without signing it. Every wiki mounts that floor through `@oracle`, which never writes. A vessel moves its floor pin only when it accepts a newer signed release. With no Nexus speaking, it stands on its last accepted floor, or on genesis. A face's wikis follow the floor of the Nexus that face stands in, so one vessel may hold two floors and never ties its faces together. An edit aimed at the floor copies up into the wiki's own working layer, and an offering back travels as a draft into the cabal's realm. A lone hearth is a Nexus of one, so its operator stands as its own Kahu. Row `W26` carries the build.
   196	* DreamDOM's ruled questions stand in <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom">> #/open-rulings.
   197	
   198	!!! Operator rulings, 2026-10-18
   199	* ''Each browser tab asks for its own unlock.'' A tab that attaches to the shared holder opens the keystore by its own ask of the person; the holder carries no unlock between tabs. The reason reads off the session law: a session wears its own face, so each tab answers for its own opening (#/rulings, a session wears the face). The ask admits a tab to its face's open hive and derives no key: the holder keeps a face's keys while some session of that face stands unlocked, and the last to close locks it (operator, 2026-10-18; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/session-unlock-2026">> #/what-both-faces-hold). Row `B1` carries the build.
   200	* ''A face's secrets never rest clear, even at a first join'' (operator, 2026-10-18, approving the house lean). A fresh device's fleet join binds a passphrase or paper slot before the join lands, since every face secret refuses to rest outside the slot tree. Row `B1`.
   201	* ''On the node, the boot marks the unlock and the session marks the face'' (operator, 2026-10-18, approving the house reading). The per-tab ask binds browser tabs; a node unlocks once per boot through its custody door, and every CLI run, MCP seat and watcher proves its own face at the gate without asking again (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/session-unlock-2026">> #/the-node-scope).
   202	* ''The last tab closes, and the browser rests at its floor'' (operator, 2026-10-18, approving the house lean). The unlock lives in page memory alone, so the browser vessel's sovereign composition ends with its last tab and the next tab asks again. Row `B1`.
   203	* ''One Keyhive identity per PersonaGroup, none above them'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-18: //"it's the only way to retain control over faces that don't know about each other"//). Each face's PersonaGroup owns its Keyhive identity, its event store, its registry, its archive and its content-key seat; no vessel-wide identity registers a face's bags, delegates them, or holds a face's group. Two faces of one vessel then never link on the wire, a removal from one face rolls that face's bags alone, and a bundle restores one face and nothing of another. Today the vessel's own identity registers every bag and delegates each face's bags through itself, and the vessel and every face share one event store and one content-key holder (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/keyhive-per-persona-group-2026">>). House readings under the operator's confidence, each naming what flips it: a herm keeps a floor-only transport key, behind a red test that it can neither author, resolve nor observe a face's capabilities, and holds no Keyhive identity if that test fails; several face hives share one process only after a substrate probe reads them isolated, and each face's hive runs in its own worker otherwise; co-mingled history migrates by fresh identities and an old mixed archive refuses by name, with no bridge; a founder that cannot leave its group leaves by a fresh PersonaGroup. Row `K15` carries the build, folding `W25` and `K12`; `W26`'s slice 3 waits on its face context.
   204	* ''A cabal shares through the faces its members choose'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-18, on the Teshima Family Council story). Kalani founds a private family council; Leilani, already standing on the DreamNet with several faces, chooses which of them join it, and a face she keeps back never learns the council exists. The council's hive reads as a Keyhive group with no key of its own: its members act through their own faces' identities, so nothing stands above them, and a presentation reads valid against the current set without naming which member made it (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/identity-classes">> #/the-handle-chain). Any current member's face promotes into the council's canon; a graft takes the threshold; a face leaves by its own act, and another's removal rides `kapae` at the threshold or a fork that omits the captor (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm">> #/the-unswept-corner); members read the owner-set as faces, never as humans. A private council declares no heraldry and lives in its members' address books under pet-names (cabal-realm #/heraldry). Row `K16` carries the story as `K15`'s acceptance.
   205	* ''The asker seals'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-19, F6's custody fork). Once the browser holder owns the Repo and the daemon kernel, it routes each sealed write to the admitted tab whose session caused it, else to any admitted, unlocked tab of that write's face; with no awake admitted tab, the write waits, named `seal-awaits-session`, never silent and never decided by a clock. No key material leaves a tab, and each sealer holds the row-class key the occupied carrier's overwrite proof opens. A SharedWorker carries no promise to run while its tabs freeze, and no `MessagePort` event reports a peer's death (round one, 2026-10-19), so a seal that waits names its wait.
   206	* ''A face's custody rows seal under its own key'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-19). Each PersonaGroup holds an independent random face custody key (FCK) that only its own slot tree opens (passphrase, paper or PRF), never wrapped under the vessel key, so a holder of the S key or of another face's unlock opens none of its rows. Face-private rows: each face's veil archive, face-key custody, guardian sets, face-provisional, the fleet-join address secret and record, a pending join bound to its target face, the per-face device shares, and each face's partition of the handle book and roster; the vessel Keyhive archive splits per PersonaGroup under `K15`. A face bundle carries that face's identity, archive, FCK recovery route and guardian set, and nothing of a sibling. Today every hot and cold custody row seals under one S key (`vault-carriers.ts`, `browser-custody.ts`), so face isolation reads as routing alone until this lands. Row `K15` carries the build, and `F6` slice three lands with its step 3. How a vessel-common act unlocks dissolves (next ruling).
   207	* ''A shared act never makes a shared secret'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-19; four ratcheted research rounds, <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/custody-per-face-2026">>). Every act that touches more than one face sorts one of three ways: its private bytes DISSOLVE into the owning face's rows (D), its public bytes stand at the FLOOR by design (F), or it names a vessel SECRET (S) whose principal and opener the house names row by row. A mixed carrier splits before it sorts. The browser holds no vessel key: founding, fleet join, slot changes, roster, archives, handle book, dyads, restore and clear sort D or F, so each tab asks only its own face's unlock and public floor work asks nothing. Phones, installed web apps, probes, the CLI, MCP and watcher seats and a native shell hold no S. A tablet waking floor carries ciphertext and public rows unattended and decrypts no face's row. A container restarts at its floor and nothing unlocks it unattended. A guest island that owns a key store stands as its own vessel. A node holds S only for rows it names: the serving key has no row yet, so it guards nothing today. * ''The place signs by a scoped signer under a pre-rotated KEL'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-19; a fifth research round, <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/custody-per-face-2026">> #/the-place-signer). A node's place identity keeps a KEL whose inception commits the next key, and that next key rides the founding card beside the seed charter's cold next key, offline; the online place signer runs unattended for an enumerated allowlist of floor duties alone (the KEL's own events excepted, which the card's key signs), rests under the host's TPM-bound credential where the host offers one and an owner-only file elsewhere, and never rides an environment, an image or a log. A stolen online signer rotates away by the card; a lost card beside a stolen signer re-founds. The floor holds no custody key; it holds its own named place signer. The format change rides the founding bake (`X0`). The place KEL commits its next cold key on the founding card and rotates by that card (`W29`), and the seed census names every reach of the seed past the floor, K15's owed bonds among them (`tools/seed-census.mjs`).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:16:role              = "face-proof — how a session proves ONE face at a gate without naming its vessel, under the PER-VESSEL shape: the face proof key per (PersonaGroup, Nexus) stays with the root-holding vessel and no private face key travels; each joined vessel mints its own face-scoped key, certified once at the join; a session signer chains beneath it. The gate reads face key → vessel's face-scoped key → session key, under one Nexus admit per face. Carries the key hierarchy, the gate exchange (a minimal Noise IK first flight in the WebSocket subprotocol token, provisional work only, a signed finish before any verdict), what the gate, a herm, a co-member and an observer each learn, the named leaks, causal deny-only withdrawal, the sibling channel's move to face scope, and what an offline root holder means"
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:30:''Two faces live from one vessel never link on the wire'' (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/persona-policy#/the-session">>). A proof that names the vessel breaks that at the first gate two sessions both dial. So a session proves itself under a ''face-scoped proof subject'', and this carrier states how that subject's keys come into being, what a gate checks, and what each party along the way learns.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:32:''Why this stands as its own carrier, beside the session contract.'' The session contract (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract">>) governs the inside of one vessel: its owner, its islands, its holder. This carrier governs the wire: a gate, a herm, a sibling and an observer read it, and none of them reads the holder's protocol. The two meet at one field, the session's proof subject, and each builds on its own order.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:45:| ''Face proof key'', one per (PersonaGroup, Nexus) | the root-holding vessel mints it at random, independent of every other key, and authorizes its public half in private causal face state | the root-holding vessel; ''its private half never travels'' | a gate sees the public half as the admitted `nym` |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:46:| ''A vessel's face-scoped key'', one per (PersonaGroup, Nexus, vessel) | the joined vessel mints it at random; the face key certifies it ONCE, at the join | that vessel's custody; its trusted daemon invokes it | a gate sees it and its certificate inside the encrypted exchange |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:47:| Session signer, one per (session, Nexus) | the vessel's daemon mints it; the vessel's face-scoped key certifies it for a dial | a session-bound handle; it drops when the session closes or switches | a gate sees its public half and its certificate inside the encrypted exchange |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:50:| Gate bundle | the gate derives separate, domain-separated transport and signing keys per (tier, Nexus, route): a floor route's from the floor key, a serving route's from the serving key, a sovereign route's from the sealed custody root (#/the-gate-exchange) | nowhere: a bundle lives in memory from a derivation to a drop; a dialer pins it per (Nexus, route) | the dialer, and anyone handed the pin |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:52:''The face's lineage re-issues the face proof key.'' The standing key and a successor minted at random both sign one hand-over; the record rides the Nexus's carriage board, the admit keeps naming the key the Nexus admitted, and a gate reads that key's line, stands a presenter under its head alone, and reads a line that forks as denied. A kapae on any key of the line holds the whole line. A gate that has not yet read the hand-over still stands the key it handed on, and no shared moment closes that gap; a compromise of the key therefore takes the face-key roll (#/causal-withdrawal), never a hand-over. A Handle card names its handle-KEL prefix, which no per-Nexus key enters, so a hand-over moves no card (house reading).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:54:''A vessel's face-scoped key never derives from, and never equals, a vessel root.'' It stands independently random per (PersonaGroup, Nexus, vessel), so no key and no certificate field repeats across two faces of one vessel. The types forbid a vessel-root key and any cross-face field in a proof.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:64:''`face key (the admitted nym)` → `the vessel's face-scoped key` → `session key`.'' The Nexus quorum admits the FACE key once per Nexus. A vessel's certificate stands as a delegate beneath that admitted face; it takes no Nexus admit of its own.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:66:''The admit proves Nexus standing; the private face grant proves PersonaGroup capability. Neither substitutes for the other.'' A gate outside the PersonaGroup needs the Nexus admit alone. A gate that shares PersonaGroup planes also asks the ring to verify the private, root-authorized grant against that face's event history. No root edge rides beside the leaf (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/membership-doctrine#/two-maps">>).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:84:''The admit's signed bytes carry the canon-document list and a validated full `GateBundlePin` for the hearth's sovereign sync route at its named Nexus. `readGateBundlePin` reads the object and its digest derives from it; the quorum's salted `carriageCommit` binds the opening inside the act image. A joinee reads the opening only through the admit at its held root (`verifySignedAdmitBundle`). Floor routes receive separate full pins through an authenticated relation or signed pin set; a floor announcement cannot authenticate its own first pin. `device-admit.ts` mints the internal `device-admit/v1` edge, and the fleet answer carries the pin and canon list.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:95:* ''The knock derives from the bundle's digest'', and the handshake's prologue holds that digest. So a gate's knock, its pin, its verdict and its posture all read per Nexus exactly, and a first flight decrypts only at the gate whose pin its dialer held.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:101:* ''An OPEN gate answers a stranger.'' A sound chain under a face no quorum admitted, presenting no arm, sorts as a stranger where this Nexus reads OPEN: the gate answers `verified`, seats it at the public shelf and keeps nothing of that face's history. Where the Nexus reads PRIVATE the same presenter draws silence. The four states that refuse (`unconfirmed`, `withdrawn`, `incomplete`, `forked`) go to a presenter of an admitted face alone.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:105:* ''Whether a hosting grant or an invite claim holds stays the sorter's own reading.'' The gate binds the arm to the face key and the Nexus, and attaches a walker only where the sorter read one.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:116:''Each derivation takes the tier, the Nexus and the route under its own name.'' No pin, key, digest or knock of one tier, one Nexus or one route links to another for an outsider: one vessel's floor pin and its sovereign pin for one Nexus share nothing.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:139:* ''It presents the contract that names that key and this gate's Nexus'': the quorum's `carry` act with the place's own carrier seal. The gate reads it through the same held-root door an admit passes, against the board's counted `uncarry` acts and the antigen, and consults the edge shadow ring for the carriage edge.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:142:* ''A standing names the presenter's own key.'' Where the sorter names a standing, for a place or for a face, it stands under the key that proved in this dial and at this gate's Nexus, or the dial draws silence.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:149:▢ ''OWED'': an operator's contract over their own herm (one signature, one place, one Nexus) names bytes no code holds yet; the arm reads the quorum's `carry` act until it does.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:183:| The Nexus gate | the stable face key AT THAT NEXUS, so it correlates that face's sessions there (ruled acceptable: two sessions of one face may correlate); the presenting vessel's face-scoped key; the session key; the presentation and its lineage; route and audience | a vessel root key, a persona root, a root edge, or the number of vessels a face holds |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:200:* ''A household TLS terminator, its log's reader, or a herm that sees the upgrade, once it holds candidate sovereign gate pins, learns which Nexus a dial selects among the K gates sharing its address and route (at most log2(K) bits per dial, none where K=1) and links that Nexus's repeat visits; the knock never tells it the presenting face, the admission verdict or any sealed byte.'' The operator's ruling of 2026-10-26 places this reader outside the sovereign route's promise. A sovereign pin escaping its members' custody, or a ruling that extends route confidentiality to pin-holders, reopens `W10` (the reading and its measurements stand at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w28-gate-lane">> #/the-knock-reading).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:210:* ''Removing one vessel withdraws ONE certificate.'' The face key signs a causal withdrawal into a ''deny-only withdrawal history'' (#/the-withdrawal-proof). A gate checks a presented chain against the withdrawals it has learned. It never consults a positive list of current vessels, and it never asks an online service whether a key still belongs. The PersonaGroup's own membership withdrawal, its rekey and the re-sealing of standing content run beside it. No face-key roll and no fresh Nexus admit follows from one vessel's removal.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:213:* ''A face-key roll'' answers a compromise of the root-held face key itself: a private causal authorization, then the affected Nexus boards' revoke and admit. No clock lapses either relation.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:223:''The face key alone authors the history.'' One history stands per face key, so one per (PersonaGroup, Nexus). Each event carries the face key, the Nexus, its position, the head of the event before it, and a digest of the withdrawn vessel's face-scoped key. The face key signs it under the withdrawal's own domain. The first event names a genesis head derived from the face key and the Nexus. No quorum signs and no board carries the history: the Nexus admitted the face key once, and a vessel's certificate stands as a delegate beneath it.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:225:''A denial names a key by digest.'' The digest binds the face key and the Nexus, so a gate that never met the vessel learns nothing of its key, and no two histories share a value. The denial covers every certificate the face key ever signs for that key. Every denial the face key signed counts wherever a reader verified it, whether or not the reader holds the events before it. ''A withdrawn key never returns'': a vessel that joins again mints a fresh key and takes a fresh certificate (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/re-admission">>).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:258:* ''One row per face key'', named by the digest that binds that face key to this Nexus, and at most 1024 events in it; a 1025th refuses. The gate reads one row for one presenter and never walks the rows. One writer moves a row at a time, and one vessel holds its store, so no two keeps lose each other's event.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:279:''Two acts remove a vessel, and each answers to its own readers.'' The dyad marker sets a device aside inside its fleet: it rides the fleet's edge board, closes the sibling lane and device sync, and moves the PersonaGroup's keys (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/four-edges">>). The certificate withdrawal denies that vessel's face-scoped key at one Nexus's gates, and rides the face's own presentations. One removal signs the dyad raise once, and one withdrawal for each face key the vessel held a certificate under. The root-holding vessel signs both, each with one signature.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:281:* ''Neither act rides a Nexus board.'' A gate reads the withdrawal and never the dyad; a sibling reads both.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:297:''A session's face names one PersonaGroup at ONE Nexus'' (house reading). The proof subject and the admit both stand per Nexus, and the session contract's face carries one of each. A face that works at two Nexuses holds one signer for each (#/the-key-hierarchy); whether one session carries both or two sessions carry one each stays the session contract's word to give.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:330:* a joined vessel keeps using the certificate it holds, under the face key the Nexus already admitted;
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:350:* ''The gate bundle'' (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/gate-bundle.ts`): the floor and sovereign tiers with their typed routes and roots (the serving tier stands owed with the ember's train E), the pin, its digest, the knock, the prologue, and the transport and signing keys one gate derives per (tier, Nexus, route). Nothing rests. Its caller: the vessel's gate composer.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:359:* ''Two custody rows.'' The face proof key rests cold with the root holder, one per (PersonaGroup, Nexus); a vessel's face-scoped key rests hot on its own vessel, one per (PersonaGroup, Nexus). Each holds 32 secret bytes and reads whole or refuses by name. The modules name the rows and the two signing doors they ask of the custody seat, and write no row.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:361:* ''The private grant's reader.'' The record that binds a face key to its PersonaGroup at one Nexus rests in the group's private causal state, and the ring reads it by vessel key today.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:365:* ''A held Nexus root per gate'': the roster, the charter lineage, the deny board and the antigen that the admit reader folds, with the causal position it read them at. A gate that holds no root refuses every admit by name.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:367:* ''The sorter over proven facts'': a class from a held admit, a private grant, the fleet reading and the arm as presented, over ONE Nexus's posture.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:380:# ''The gate, behind interfaces.'' Specified in code, with the bundle's root, the held Nexus root, the rings by face key and the sorter over proven facts owed.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:3:<<^ code="&#x0001;" namespace="⊙" from="?" -> to="lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm">>
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:8:file-path         = "bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem"
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:17:role              = "cabal-realm — a CabalGroup read as an IMAGINED REALM on the DreamNet: the superset of the members' shared infrastructure, imagined as one shared expanse (a hearth beside, not a category above). It carries no DID of its own — a Place bears identity, a vessel names the metal running the code, a realm names what the members jointly imagine and maintain. Named-not-ruled, alive by its epoch, dissolving to anu when unfed. The tie-break rides the realm's epoch (BeeKEM); malice rides Plane-B convergent-removal. GOVERNING A REALM ⊥ GOVERNING THE METAL (operator ruling 2026-08-09): the Ostrom principles govern the realm — the virtual relationship-place — while infrastructure authority (who runs the metal, who holds the archive passphrase, who lights a Herm, who signs a kāpae) sits on the vessel and the charter. Neither substitutes for the other"
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:19:title             = "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm"
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:21:uri-path          = "ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm"
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:28:A ''CabalGroup'' (the multi-human social tier above the PersonaGroups) reads as ''an imagined realm on the DreamNet: the superset of the members' shared infrastructure, represented as one imagined expanse.'' Not a //super-category// — a containing class with members as a subset, top-down, needing a root admitter — but ''a realm the members agree to share and maintain'': a realm ''drawn by the relationships, which dissolves if they break.'' The Crossroads shrine of the fiction (a district hearth fed by collective offering), made literal.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:30:''The word cuts three ways, and the cuts hold apart'' (operator ruling): a ''Place'' bears identity — the hearth that holds a DID. A ''vessel'' names the metal currently running the code. A ''realm'' names neither: it names ''what the members jointly imagine over their pooled vessels and Places'', a superset no single machine hosts and no single key signs. The realm never mints a DID; it composes the members' own.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:43:A group never holds you the way a //container// does (a noun — a membership-list, needing a root admitter, a single point of capture). It runs as ''a thing you continuously DO'' (a verb). The commons historians name it exactly: //"there is no commons without commoning — the commons is a verb."// Members do not ''belong to'' the cabal; they ''maintain'' it. Inversion of control, reified as a commons. The realm holds imagined precisely because the maintaining, never a host, sustains it.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:45:''What the maintaining DEPOSITS'' — `nohopapa` (ʻōlelo Hawaiʻi: to dwell in one place across generations; settling into a foundation, layer, rank, structured sequence). The verb names the doing; `nohopapa` names what the doing ''accrues''. A member does not hold a grant that expires — they ''dwell in the realm, and the dwelling deposits `papa` — a settled depth''. Stop dwelling and no deed remains to lapse; the depth ''erodes''. So the model carries no lease anywhere: a lease makes a substance-object you hold between exercises, and this stack refuses that shape. (Refused deliberately: `hoʻolimalima`, the modern land-transaction lease-term — it entered the language through the machinery by which Hawaiian land left Hawaiian hands, and a stack whose brief reads ''shelter against empire'' does not name its primitive after that instrument.)
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:47:''Composition runs BOTH ways.'' A realm holds what its dwellers dwell ''in'' — so the realm sustaining its members never reads as a second leg bolted onto the constructor; ''being-dwelt-in makes it a realm''. A realm that does nothing for its members' standing fails a condition the ontology imposes, never merely a courtesy it skipped.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:49:But the Mu cuts both ways: a ''verb-realm carries a defended noun-boundary.'' Drop the boundary (Ostrom P1) and the verb-realm either //starves// (false dissolution) or gets //captured//. The surviving shape: ''a verb that keeps a boundary.''
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:53:<<~ ahu #/convening-and-cabal>>
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:64:''A council logs into their devices, signs an Act, and disperses — and whether they sat together in one room never enters it.'' The convening dissolves by design. ''The Cabal does not dissolve with it'', because the Cabal names the relations rather than the gathering, and this meme has always said so: the relationships define the realm, and it ends ''when they break'' — never when they stop meeting.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:74:<<~ ahu #/the-realm>>
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:78:* ''NAMED, not ruled'' — the realm's identity rides ''content-addressed'' (its genesis CID, #GEN_2) — a name, never a DID, and never a root. The name grants no //authority// (#ISLAND_4, DocUrl-not-authority) — but, crucible-corrected, it grants no //privacy// either: a stable realm-id advanced by a same-key signed pointer carries a public ''linkability + timing surface'' — existence, version-history, activity cadence, and (via epoch-rotation timing) membership-change events leak to any reader even with the roster veiled (Pfitzmann-Hansen · PURBs). A name carries no root; it does carry a trackable handle.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:79:* ''RULED by the closure'' — authority runs as the ''closure of mutual maintenance edges'' (`group-as-closure`: "no central object, evaluated as a query, never instantiated"). The doc is the shared ''substrate''; the relationships are the ''authority''. Share substrate, not sovereignty (`causal-islands.mem`) — each member keeps their own vessel-key, and the realm borrows none of them.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:80:* ''LIVED by its epoch'' — the realm carries its ''own epoch/lease'', the collective-maintenance heartbeat. ''Own'' reads as an ADDRESS, not only a sense — and ''#112's ruling lands here as a fence, not only as a seat''. The realm's epoch reads as its ''feed'', the heartbeat the members keep together, which must take a peer's write. The ''admission fence'' beside it — the signed lease epoch (`quorum-lease`: the charter quorum's advances, folded by maximum) a grant binds with `boundEpoch` (#94) — bounds outstanding invites, and ''admission belongs to infrastructure management'': it sits on the ''vessel and the cabal'', never in the realm. The two share a doc id ''BY CONSTRUCTION, never by debt'': a cabal names the shared relation over its realm's resources (a community — forum, server, group — read as the humans behind its shared Handle cloud), so identity-as-relation names it by that realm's doc. ''One name reads pono; one SLOT did not.'' ⚠ ''MEASURED, addressed alike they collapse to ONE SLOT'' and each drives the other — //feeding a realm staled its own invites, and revoking an invite read as maintenance//. Both fold by MAX and neither verifies a seal before folding, so a board carrying both hands any peer a revocation over resources it holds no authority on. They now hold ''separate address spaces''; the feed carries ''no daemon root'' and rides whichever board holds it. <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/epoch-binding-surfaces">>
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:81:* ''DISSOLVED by cooling'' — break the maintenance and the realm ''cools to anu'' (the residency model) — it //never deletes// (a hard-deleted CRDT item a peer still holds flows back and resurrects); it goes cold, re-warmable. //A fed node hums, a neglected one flickers.//
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:87:!! The Tie-Break ~ the realm's epoch (BeeKEM), not a person
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:89:The held multi-principal key-handover break — concurrent add-while-remove leaks a key, equal peers, no senior to order it — resolves ''in the realm, not a person'': the realm's epoch carries it, ''exactly the MLS pattern lifted to decentralized causal-order CGKA'' (DCGKA · causal TreeKEM · ''BeeKEM — already on our stack via Keyhive''). Concurrent membership ops ''converge by deterministic blank-on-merge'' — concurrent leaves sorted, racing paths blanked, replicas agree on tree //shape// — //no human adjudicates the merge.// Coordinator-free, no kahu, no smuggled root. But, crucible-corrected, ''converge ≠ heal'': after a concurrent merge the tree holds //no root secret// until a later ''non-concurrent'' commit lands — the no-root-secret window; the merge ''defers, never delivers'', post-compromise security (Bienstock-Dodis-Rösler: PCS cost grows with concurrency degree).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:96:''OPEN ~ which fold the realm's heartbeat rides.'' `first-realm-arc#/what-the-runbook-lacks` reads a realm's standing as per-writer slots folded by MAX, a fold that picks a winner. This section holds that concurrent rolls of the keying epoch merge by blanking, and #/verb-not-noun holds that the model carries no lease. No ruling settles which fold the feed takes; both readings stand listed (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/first-realm-arc#/what-the-runbook-lacks">>).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:104:Without these the realm becomes the //un//-governed commons that collapses (Hardin), not the Ostrom commons that endures. ''MUST ride:''
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:108:* ''P2 — benefit ∝ maintenance.'' The realm remembers who fed it; defeats free-riding.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:109:* ''Soft-state discipline'' — a generous re-warm K-factor (so a still-wanted realm doesn't falsely starve) + bounded cold-GC by causal stability (so tombstones don't bloat every replica forever).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:113:''Two managements wear one word, and a reading that fuses them mis-sites every seat it names'' (operator ruling). A realm stands as a ''virtual relationship-place'' — what the members jointly imagine over their pooled vessels; its governance follows Ostrom, and its subject spans the shared expanse. ''Infrastructure management'' takes a different subject entirely: who runs which metal, who holds the archive passphrase, who lights a Herm into a lararium, who signs a Nexus kāpae. Those seats sit on the vessel and the charter, never in the realm.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:115:The fusion comes easily because the same person often does both, and it fails in one direction: ''a realm's members agreeing something does NOT move a key, and an operator holding the metal does NOT hold a vote in the realm.'' Where a design needs both it must name both, separately — the realm's agreement and the infrastructure's authority never substitute for each other.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:117:The Ostrom principles above still hold ''unchanged'' under the cut; they govern the realm. Read them as claims about the metal and P1's cost-dial turns into an admission fee for hardware, which no one ever ruled.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:123:!! The house table ~ a shared realm, a referee-private bag, and self-blinding by recipe
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:125:''A tabletop table reads as a table cabal with a shared realm, plus a referee-private bag'' (operator-approved model, 2026-10-11). The model takes the house's own RPG table as its worked case, and it teaches the planes at kitchen-table scale.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:127:* ''The table realm'' holds what every seat at the table shares.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:141:''The house's own worked example'': `bags/elyncia` holds the table realm and `bags/elyncia-referee` holds the referee's bag. A player face's recipe mounts the first; the referee face's recipe mounts both.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:145:''OWED'': no leaf yet honours a session's effective recipe; an admitted leaf reads its hearth's default recipe. A table's own realm stands as a cabal realm beside the Nexus's (#/many-realms).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:149:<<~ ahu #/many-realms>>
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:151:!! Many realms under one Nexus ~ a verb names its realm
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:153:> ''Operator ruling.'' CABAL names the collective, REALM holds shared resources, NEXUS names the federated hardware mesh. An operator's offering to a book club belongs in that club's realm, signed by the face worn there.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:155:''A vessel stands one plane per realm.'' Two kinds stand:
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:157:|! realm |! its name |! who reads its documents |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:158:| ''the charter-derived realm'' | the Nexus's own AID, the charter's genesis epoch | the charter's hearth, the registration's own hands, and each contracted member of the Nexus |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:159:| ''a cabal realm'' | 64 hex, the name its vouch board and its feed already wear | a peer that holds lineage standing in that realm, and nobody else |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:161:* ''A verb names its realm.'' `lares nexus realm-bag`, `realm-bags` and the meme verbs take `--realm <id>`. With none named, a verb routes to the charter-derived realm. A verb that names a realm reads that realm alone: no other realm's registration answers, and the vessel's own bag of that name never stands in.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:162:* ''A write to one realm never appears in another's plane.'' Each realm keeps its own shared doc, its own standing registrations, its own steward pin and its own gate.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:163:* ''An act stands the vessel in a realm; a read never does.'' Registering, asking and consenting in a cabal realm stand its plane and note the realm in the vessel's own ledger. Naming a realm the vessel never entered reads empty.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:164:* ''A cabal takes no key and no roster.'' Standing in a cabal realm reads as a live query over its vouch lineage (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/reach">>). The plane holds no member list, and a steward's key there derives against the Nexus the realm stands under.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:165:* ''A realm stands under one charter, a seed's or a Nexus's'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-18; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/edge-hands">>). A council that meets at one hearth stands under its seed charter, and one two hearths carry stands under the Nexus they found. The vessel's own ledger keeps the charter its first act there named. The planes stand each realm the ledger notes under the charter that stands here, or under none yet; a realm noted under another charter stands no plane here, and an act that would enter it refuses `realm-under-another-nexus`.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:166:* ''A Nexus member outside a cabal reads nothing of its realm.'' The Nexus lane and the charter-hearth lane answer for the charter-derived realm alone. A contracted carrier still carries a cabal realm's PUBLIC-tier book by hash.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:167:* ''Wire access attaches to the document, never to the record that named it.'' Where the vessel's own steward keeps a book in some realm, those realms alone answer for it: a record another hand wrote in another realm neither opens that book nor shuts it. A book two answering realms both hold crosses to a peer every one of them admits. The vessel's own hand in a realm reads as the name its steward pin holds there, the face it last sealed with.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:168:* ''A registration widens who reads a book and never narrows it.'' Whatever the vessel already carries to every peer, its public and infrastructure planes, stays carried once a realm registers it.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:169:* ''The daemon island reads its own vessel's verdict.'' The plane folds each realm's standing registrations and rests the verdict on the vessel's own plane; the island reads that and folds nothing. A Nexus the vessel leaves takes every realm's pins and verdict along, a stand that fails leaves none, and a verdict with no doc pin beside it answers nothing.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:171:''OWED.'' A cabal realm's documents cross between two operators only once the realm's member consult answers for a peer, and that consult reads the node's root map, which nothing fills. The vouch door and the member edge name the key a worn face presents to the Nexus. The consult still waits on two things: a socket that proves that key per Nexus (the wire train's face-scoped proof subject), and how a seat-holder's face stands in a realm once chairs sign with seat keys (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/what-the-code-holds">>).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:179:> ''Operator ruling.'' A scoped face signs acts that belong to one person; a transparent quorum Handle signs acts the collective owns; the root never appears publicly. A human wears many faces and many public Handles, each in many cabals, and signs a steward edge with the face or Handle worn in that cabal.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:181:''A realm record publishes whatever key it names.'' A realm-bag registration names its stewards in `keptBy`. The realm doc crosses to every member, and the `@crossroads` announce names `keptBy` on the public plane. So a steward's name reads one of two classes and nothing else:
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:184:| ''face'' | the key the steward's worn face presents at the Nexus the realm stands under | that key signs the record's own bytes |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:187:* ''One door picks the key.'' A vessel's steward door hands out the key its worn face presents to that Nexus, and nothing else (`packages/lararium-node/src/realm-steward.ts`). A vessel that wears no face refuses by name. No option names a persona index, and no roster order picks a face.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:188:* ''A guard stands before every seal.'' The door and the realm plane each read the signer's key against the vessel's own keys. A persona root, a vessel key, a key the vessel cannot class and a vault that will not read each refuse by name.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:189:* ''A name enters a record by its own hand first.'' No vessel can class a key that belongs to another hand, and no roster of face keys stands to ask: the carriage board records carriage, never belonging. So a hand that would keep a bag another hand keeps ASKS from its own vessel, sealing with its own worn face a record that names the standing stewards and itself; each standing steward then consents with her own. A keeping hand names another steward only where that name already sealed a record of the realm.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:193:* ''The widest consented set stands.'' Counted records for one bag that agree on the doc fold to the one whose `keptBy` holds every other's: each wider record carries the narrower one's stewards' own seals. Two docs under one name tie, and so do two steward sets where neither holds the other; a tie leaves the bag unregistered and grants no write. Any realm member who writes a rival counted record can force that tie.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:200:* ''Every hand in a realm takes this key.'' The vouch door signs a vouch with it (`cabal-vouch.ts`), so a vouch edge's id and a member edge's id name it; an edge's holder hand on a realm's board signs with it (`edge-kapae-cmd.ts`); and the feed's writer and the crossing's applicant read it through one door (`cabal-face.ts`, `lares cabal face`, `feed`, `join`). No verb names a persona index, and none reaches a root: a person wears the face that acts.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:210:The one failure mode with ''no off-the-shelf fix'', named so it stays visible: ''liveness-by-maintenance rewards PERSISTENCE, not LEGITIMACY.'' A small hostile faction can ''out-maintain an apathetic majority and keep a captured realm as theirs'' — soft-state has no defense, it rewards whoever keeps feeding. The realm dissolves when //everyone// abandons it, never when the //wrong// hands keep it warm.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:213:* ''Fork-as-exit (primary) — BUILT + witnessed'' (`fork-realm.ts` + real-Keyhive probe): the legitimate maintainers carry the realm's membership into a ''fresh sentinel realm'' that ''excludes the captors by OMISSION'' (build-corrected: a fork names a realm you LEAVE, so no hand ever adds the captors to the fresh sentinel — no membership key — cleaner than convergent-removal, which evicts from a realm you KEEP; the Steem→Hive airdrop-exclusion made native). Each vessel ''re-points its own petname'' to the fork (Zooko: the id changing makes the feature — no global consensus, no admitter), and the fork records ''forkedFrom'' for continuity. //Witnessed: the captor's `verifySentinelMembership` reads FALSE on the fork; the survivors' TRUE.// Hirschman's bound: exit disciplines a captor //only while forking stays cheap// — so the build must lower switching cost, or the cure plays as theatre.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:214:* ''A capture-clock, not a gate — BUILT'' (`cabal-realm-clock.ts`): surface //who feeds the realm and since when// (free; the liveness signal already kept) so the majority ''sees'' a minority out-feeding them //while it happens//, while exit still runs cheap. Verdict-free — the operator calibrates the threshold.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:217:''THE CLOCK READS RIVALS, and its limit has a name.'' A single clock reports one replica's sighting; the honest instrument runs ''N independent readings over one declared realm with the spread published'', treating divergence as the signal rather than reconciling it — the shape both interlaboratory comparison and rival reference-frame realizations arrive at, neither needing a rung above. ''And no separation of roles cures a paid reader'': across seven canonical failures in a field that formalised the split for a century, six kept it perfectly and failed anyway, on the invariant that ''whoever pays the gauge bends the gauge''.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:219:''What `nohopapa` changes here, and what it does NOT.'' It does not dissolve the hard-bound — legitimacy still cannot live in the join-gate, and a captured realm still reads live to any liveness signal. It changes ''what the capture-clock can see''. Bare maintenance reports a rate; depth-in-a-layer reports a ''stratum'' — who has dwelt, how deep, and through how many turns of the realm's own rhythm. A faction that out-feeds an apathetic majority ''this season'' still shows shallow against dwellers who have settled through many; a faction that has genuinely dwelt long has, by the model's own lights, ''become'' maintainers. So the clock gains a second axis and the corner stays unswept — sight sharpens, prevention does not arrive. The same shape answers //diligence ≠ title// one layer down, at a hearth's carriage for its walkers: a guest's own rhythm sets the measure, presence earns notice before reclaim, and the hearth's quota and roll keep title where it was (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/membership-doctrine#/the-walkers-carriage">>).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:221:This stays ''OPEN — the operator's design seat'': the residual reads as calibration (how cheap the fork must run · how the petname re-point coordinates at scale — the Schelling-point risk), and the honest hard-bound that the design makes capture ''survivable + visible, never prevented''. Every shrine keeps one unswept corner; this one belongs to the cabal.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:229:A cabal-realm shares content without materializing a reader-set. It seals each post to the ''NP-predicate'' //"holder presents a valid delegation-chain to the charter root, valid for epoch e"// — the ''same witness'' the maintenance-closure already reads (`group-as-closure`) — so ''the two planes collapse onto one cap-chain'': the chain that authorizes maintenance IS the decryption witness. No reader-object stands; //"who may read?"// reads ''unanswerable by design'' (a predicate's extension, never a list). The group-messaging trilemma (strong-PCS · efficient fan-out · no materialized set — pick two) ''dissolves as scoped'': the set never forms (horn 3), one ciphertext-trace diffuses by gossip (horn 2), and post-compromise HEALING lands at ''epoch cadence'' — the substrate ceiling, since strong-immediate healing would demand a global-now the causal-island law forbids (//you cannot lose what the substrate never permitted//). Forward-secrecy rides epoch-time; healing rides the ''same short-TTL cap + revoke-CID G-set that ages the closure'' — one evaporation-trace, both planes (Ledger-State Stigmergy). Deploy floor: ''Silent Threshold Encryption'' today, ramping to ''Witness Encryption''; never CP-ABE/IBE/DKG (a coordinator smuggles a global-now back in). Five domains converged on the one attractor — witness-encryption · clonal-selection · stigmergy · CRDT-as-sheaf (`cohomological-gate`) · the color-manifold honesty-brake (//the unwrap-witness relocates, never vanishes//). ''Carriage keeps the same shape'': the subject PRESENTS its quorum-signed admit at the wire, and the gate checks it against a deny-only board — no allow roster forms there either (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/kahu#/nexus-scale">>).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:253:''ONE JOINT REMAINS, and it reads as the one that mattered'': the split runs through STORAGE, never through AUTHORITY. No threshold, quorum or signature gates any of the three writes, and one operator command still moves ''kahu and seal together'' — a fusion the ruling forbids and the code still owes. ''The kahu quorum (the seal lineage, k-of-n) and the engine CADENCE stand as separate joints'': a cadence threshold seated apart from the kahu quorum — a self-governing lineage with its own inception, its own per-seat pre-rotation and its own seat events, held by those who bear the reboot cost (operators whose places run the engine) — offers the engine and advances the Nexus's rolling window of admitted engines; each device moves only by its own adoption; the kahu quorum never offers an engine, and the cadence threshold never admits anyone. The grammar holds no cadence at all — it lives by use (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/kahu#/contract">>). So the warning this section opens with stands undischarged — //a quorum that rotates keys can silently move the admission price// — because the costs that differ by orders still answer to one hand. Splitting the ceremony is the next act, and it waits on the FORUM below: a threshold gate names who may object, and nobody has said who holds standing.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:267:''So the Face carries'': a chosen name · a mark · a bearing · pointers a stranger may fetch. ''And it carries no roster, no count, and no member identity'' — the shore that projects it reads only {realm, meta} and could not carry more if a later hand wanted it to.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:271:''A sealed collective loses no self.'' One with no public face and no signed leyline stays fully itself — severable because rendezvous ≠ identity, so no seizable object stands (the shelter-against-empire shape, #/verb-not-noun). Opening a door later stays cheap: sign a carriage contract and `#has-NOT {read}` survives it; across a DIFFERENT engine two sealed realms interoperate only at the content-address floor (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/nexus-topology">> #/the-severability-law).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm.mem:279:A cabal splits at ''two roots'' (operator ruling). A ''private-held root'' — the members' own persona-clouds + private closure, causal-island-local, content predicate-keyed (#/the-seal), unlinkable by the per-circle scope-pseudonym. And a ''public org root'' published to ''@crossroads'' (the public plane): a ''charter-epoch lineage'' whose ''head'' names the current co-joined membership surface (//the set is mortal// — present state), and whose ''posted data carries a wax-stamp that attests a PAST'' (#/the-wax-stamp), carrying the pledged-Handle's public DID, claimed deliberately, one-way. The public reach costs ''no global-now'': the surface never composes into a per-citizen registry to scrape. This ''resolves the linkability-surface'' the stable realm-id otherwise leaks (#/the-realm) — the public face shows the moment, never the trail. Kowloon Circles thus separate into private-held roots + public org roots — the veil-ladder's overlay/floor made a two-root cut (`the-veil-ladder`).

