4. **Device and dispatch** — F10/G13. Reds: removed/stale device, forged writer, cross-layer tombstone and restart replay refuse; control: retained device/current working intent; positive: explicit causal removal, durable lease/fence/dedup and outcome. Holds fleet view/removal UI, summons/dispatcher, effect index/reader. K15 supplies face verification; D2 projection is consumer only. Fleet and intent genesis bytes before bake.
5. **I2 far-agent relay** — independent lane, separately scouted; after I1 and relay interface freeze. Red: revoked/altered delegation or relay-minted face act refuses; control: valid delegation and intact arguments; positive: relay admits intent while face device signs the act. Holds the I2 relay/admission files per scout handback. Separate relay key, never K15 carriage identity. Genesis grant/relay formats before bake.

