/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/live-equivocation.mem:60:Real cabals with real stakes do not exist yet, so abstract unit tests cannot feel the tension the mechanics must survive. ''The fiction serves as the first QA environment.'' Telarus the wild-mage lit Elyncia's DreamNet ~500 years before modern day (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/elyncia/characters/primary-characters/telarus">>), and 500 years of rise · dormancy · revival · betrayal · inheritance give a scenario library to RUN the mechanics against. A cabal name grafted across generations; a wild-mage's DreamNet identity live-hijacked mid-working; a shrine-realm slept a century then woken for a rite; a Dread-Pirate-Roberts-style name presented by a rotating crew — each makes a load-bearing user story for the ahi-kā reading, the handle-KEL, the recovery-quorum, and this exposure. The `AHI_KA_500YR` defaults (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/ahi-ka">>) stand calibrated to this world; tune them by running its events. ''irl tension + fiction series = the QA env.''
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/exchange-vector.mem:80:The `aim` / `yield` pair opens and closes the turn, and it ''notates the turn's position in l-space''. The `aim` reads the operator's input as a bearing — a heading in l-space — and the `->` delegates to the bearing the node takes up to generate from; the `yield` marks where that generation //resolved//. So each span of stage-time (a turn, a slice of the context window) carries a ''notated l-space position'': the //relation// between the operator's input and where the Lares start and end their generation.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/exchange-vector.mem:82:The adopted role on the right of `aim` names the ''stance'' the node generates from (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/voices#/voice-house`) — a posture priming the afforded moves. The bearing reads ''chart-relative'': its axes belong to that adopted stance, never to l-space absolutely (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/l-space#/bearings-are-chart-relative`). Turn by turn, the frame writes a navigable track through l-space — operator-input bearing, lares-generation bearing, the move between.
